`ifndef HISI_RTC_SPI_V3_RDL
`define HISI_RTC_SPI_V3_RDL

regfile eHISI_RTC_SPI_INTERNAL_V3 {
    name = "HiSilicon SPI-bridged RTC (internal registers, Hi3516A V200 family layout with battery low-voltage detection)";
    desc = "
    Internal (SPI-bridged) register space of the RTC of the **Hi3516A V200, Hi3519 V101, Hi3516C V300 / Hi3516E V100 and Hi3516A V300** (36 byte-wide registers). The offsets are **SPI internal addresses** (`spi_add`,
    0-127, of `SPI_RW` in the APB part `eHISI_RTC_SPI`); this is not a CPU address space. It is the Hi3518E V20X map `eHISI_RTC_SPI_INTERNAL_V2` (0x00-0x18 counters / match / load / lock / interrupts / clock / POR,
    0x51-0x5A SDM coefficients and user registers, no temperature-compensation LUT) plus **battery low-voltage (under-voltage, UV) detection**: a second interrupt source `*_uv` next to the timing interrupt in
    RTC_IMSC / RTC_MSC_INT / RTC_RAW_INT, a global enable `rtc_imsc` [2], and the control register RTC_UV_CTRL at 0x1A (enable, filtered / unfiltered source, 1 s .. 30 min detection period). The Hi3520D register
    RTC_SAR_CTRL (0x1A, temperature update period) does not exist on these chips.

    Counter: RTC_10MS_COUNT 0x00 .. RTC_D_COUNT_H 0x05 (read-only 40-bit up counter at 100 Hz: 10 ms [6:0] 0-99, seconds 0-59, minutes 0-59, hours 0-23, days 16-bit); while `rtc_lock_bypass` is 0 the count registers only
    update after a lock (write RTC_LORD = 0x2, poll until it reads 0, wait 1 ms, then read 0x00-0x05: DS 3.9.4.5 of the Hi3516A V300 edition). Match (alarm) value RTC_MR_* 0x06-0x0B (reset all ones), load value RTC_LR_* 0x0C-0x11,
    loaded into the counter by RTC_LORD.rtc_load = 1 (wait 10 ms). RTC soft reset: write 0 to RTC_POR_N and wait 30 ms.

    **SPI_RW protocol (DS 3.9.4.5):** wait until SPI_RW bit 31 (`spi_busy`) is 0; write `spi_start` (bit 24) | `spi_rw` (bit 23: 0 = write, 1 = read) | `spi_add` [22:16] | `spi_wdata` [7:0]; for a read poll `spi_busy` and take SPI_RW[15:8].
    (The data sheet read example `0x01860000` has bit 23 set although the text says `spi_rw is 0`: DS text error, inherited from the Hi3518E V20X edition.)

    Sources: Hi3516A V200 data sheet issue 01 section 3.9.7 (`hi3516av200--Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` lines 13757-14760; the citations below), checked register by register (names, offsets, bit ranges, access, resets) against the
    Hi3519 V101 (`hi3519v101--Hi3519V101-Datasheet.txt` lines 13701-14703), Hi3516C V300 / Hi3516E V100 (`hi3516cv300--Hi3516CV300-Hi3516EV100-Datasheet.txt` lines 13222-14224) and the original Chinese Hi3516A V300 user guide
    (`hi3516av300--Hi3516AV300-Datasheet.txt` lines 16530-17381: identical map; the Hi3516A V300 APB side has no temperature-sensor registers, see `eHISI_RTC_SPI`): all four agree. Data-sheet only, not hardware verified; no vendor
    driver source (the vendor `hi_rtc` driver is closed-source MPP code).
    ";

    reg {
        name = "Count value register for the RTC 10 ms counter";
        desc = "RTC_10MS_COUNT is a count value register for the RTC 10 ms counter.

Data sheet 3.9.7 RTC_10MS_COUNT (internal address 0x00, printed page 3-180, `hi3516av200--Hi3516AV200-Datasheet.txt` line 13762).";
        regwidth = 8;

        field {
            name = "rtc_10ms_count";
            desc = "RTC 10 ms counter value. It indicates the currently counted time. Its unit is 10 ms. The value range is 0-99.";
            sw = r;
            hw = w;
            reset = 0x0;
        } rtc_10ms_count[6:0];
    } RTC_10MS_COUNT @ 0x0;

